course: dictionary
lesson: 10658
title: Adverbs that show how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unkindly is an adverb. An adverb tells us how, when or where something happens, and it often ends in -ly. Unkindly comes from kind, with un- (not) added to the front and -ly at the end. It means in a way that is not kind, not caring, or a bit cruel.
explain: Look at the words next to it. «Speak unkindly» tells us how someone talked, and «treat someone unkindly» tells us how someone acted. In both, the reader knows a character is being mean or hurtful. Ask yourself: how did they do it? The adverb usually answers that.
explain: Be careful with «don't take it unkindly». Here the phrase means don't be offended. The writer is saying, "I did not mean to hurt you." The example «lǎoye («LAOW-yeh») is grandad on mum's side in the north; in the south he is wàigōng, where wài means outside, from an old custom families today do not mean unkindly.» shows the same idea: the families do not mean to be hurtful.
fact: Unkindly means in a way that is not kind.
fact: «Speak unkindly» means to talk in a hurtful way, and «treat someone unkindly» means to act in a mean or cruel way.
fact: «Don't take it unkindly» means don't be offended.
fact: Adverbs like unkindly tell us how, when or where something happens.
fact: Kindly is the opposite of unkindly.
exercise: «She spoke unkindly to her little brother.» What does unkindly tell us? | When she spoke, in the morning | *How she spoke, in a mean way | Where she was standing | Who she was talking to
exercise: «The lady treated the new girl unkindly.» Find and copy the one word that is an adverb meaning in a way that is not kind. | *unkindly | treated | girl | new
exercise: «Don't take it unkindly, I didn't mean to upset you.» What does don't take it unkindly mean? | *Don't be offended | Don't pay for it | Don't hurry away | Don't be happy about it
test: «The boys laughed unkindly at the boy who fell over.» What is the closest meaning of unkindly? | Happily | Quietly | Quickly | *Meanly, in a cruel way
test: Which word is the opposite of unkindly? | *Kindly | Loudly | Badly | Sadly
exam: In «from an old custom families today do not mean unkindly», what does unkindly show? | Families are very old | *Families are not trying to hurt or be mean | Families are cross with each other | Families are very loud
